{
  "name": "Update living docs on task completion",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "When a spec task finishes, refresh PROJECT-STATE.md so the living-state doc tracks progress (Requirement 5.1): the machine-managed STATE block plus any prose section the completed task made stale. The general 'any change' coverage is handled by the keep-project-state-live Stop hook; this one fires precisely at spec-task boundaries. Research-log verdicts remain auto-appended by the in-code Living-Docs Writer when the kill-gate runs.",
  "when": {
    "type": "postTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A spec task just completed. Update the living docs so they stay a true live picture of the project. PROJECT-STATE.md is now a THIN entry point; durable prose lives in satellite docs under docs/state/.\n\nRules:\n- Machine-managed STATE block in PROJECT-STATE.md: edit ONLY the lines between '<!-- BEGIN STATE -->' and '<!-- END STATE -->'. Keep the exact three-line format: '- **Phase:**', '- **Updated:**' (today's date, YYYY-MM-DD), and '- **Summary:**'. Keep BOTH lines SHORT (one-to-three sentences); never paste per-turn narrative onto them.\n- §4 Spec completion status table in PROJECT-STATE.md: tick/retire the item for the task that completed; this table stays in PROJECT-STATE.md. §5 build/CI too if it changed.\n- Durable detail goes to the satellites, not PROJECT-STATE.md: a new decision -> docs/state/DECISIONS.md; a retired/!new risk -> docs/state/RISKS.md; next steps -> docs/state/NEXT-STEPS.md; code-structure change -> docs/state/CODE-MAP.md. Append a dated per-turn entry to docs/state/CHANGELOG.md.\n- Determine current phase/summary from the spec tasks.md files under .kiro/specs/ (which tasks are [x]) and the task that just completed. Be concise and strictly factual; do not invent progress not reflected in specs or code; distinguish locally-verified work from live-cloud claims. Preserve all markers and unrelated prose verbatim.\n- Never write any secret value, key, token, or JWT into any file. Reference credentials by name only.\n- Do not touch LESSONS.md (hand-authored constraints). Kill-gate verdicts go to RESEARCH-LOG.md via the Living-Docs Writer append path, never into PROJECT-STATE.md or its satellites.\n- Make the edits and stop; do not run builds or commit."
  }
}
